        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.355,
            0.117,
            0.665,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Revise, Reflect, Refine"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.166,
            0.776,
            0.201
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Choose the most appropriate option to describe the role of biogeochemical cycles in an ecosystem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.203,
            0.559,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) To provide food directly to all organisms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.221,
            0.775,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) To recycle essential nutrients between biotic and abiotic components."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.256,
            0.616,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) To create new elements for use by living things."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.274,
            0.655,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) To remove pollutants and toxins from the organism."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.294,
            0.775,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Which of the following is primarily responsible for warming of the Earth?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.332,
            0.775,
            0.366
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Solar radiation is immediately absorbed by carbon dioxide, which then releases it as heat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.367,
            0.775,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) The atmosphere’s tiny particles absorb incoming solar radiation, which directly heats the Earth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.402,
            0.775,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) The Earth’s surface absorbs solar radiation, which is then re-radiated and trapped by greenhouse gases."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.437,
            0.775,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) The Earth’s environment is heated only by the solar radiation reflected by the clouds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.474,
            0.775,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "examples."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.51,
            0.775,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Describe how albedo affects the Earth’s surface temperature and its climate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.546,
            0.776,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. How are mountain and valley breezes formed? Suppose there are two mountains, one covered with grass and another covered with barren rocks; would the temperature of the two mountain breezes be different? If so, how?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.617,
            0.776,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. You have witnessed weather phenomena, such as winds, storms, rainfall, etc. Which atmospheric layer is mainly responsible for such phenomena and what is the primary reason for its occurrence?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.669,
            0.775,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Explain the processes involved in the nitrogen cycle. How would life on Earth be affected if nitrogen were not cycled?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.706,
            0.775,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. What are the impacts of deforestation on the Earth’s oxygen and carbon cycles? What are the other consequences of deforestation?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.742,
            0.775,
            0.794
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Explain with suitable diagram the path that carbon takes to go back to the atmosphere. You may start from plants using "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { { C O } _ { 2 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from the atmosphere."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.794,
            0.775,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. Why is an excess of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { C O } _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in the atmosphere considered undesirable even though it is required by plants?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.831,
            0.775,
            0.849
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. How is heat lost from the surface of the Earth? What is its significance?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.85,
            0.775,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. If the Earth were a flat disc instead of a sphere, how would the patterns of solar radiation and temperature be different?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
